<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Skin</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Ranger (guild level 2), Druid (guild level 12, up to 80%)
Also taught by: Ben the skin trader, at his trading post in Udgaard (anyone, up to 50%); Mary the Lumberjack Wife, in her cabin in the forest of Haon-Dor (anyone, up to 50%, once you have brought back her cooking pot); Gustav, in the back room of the inn in Udgaard (anyone, up to 35%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>skin corpse
</pre>
<p>Takes the hide, fur or scales from a corpse. Sell it for money, or keep 
it as a trophy. You need a dagger to do it, carried or wielded, and it 
costs endurance, more for a big beast. You must be standing.
</p><p>Your skill and dexterity decide how well it goes, against the creature's 
level: the mightier the beast, the harder its skin is to take cleanly. A 
fine skin from a rare creature is worth a good deal. Botch it, and the 
skin is mangled by your knife and you get nothing. Either way, a corpse can only be 
skinned once. Some creatures have no skin worth taking. Practising it 
needs dexterity 10.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
